{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471176-effects-of-the-embrace-and-regeneration","id":1471176,"title":"Effects of the Embrace and regeneration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-23T22:09:12-08:00","id":1471176,"title":"Effects of the Embrace and regeneration","content":"So something that I had been thinking about, in V5 there is little to no information on the effects of the Embrace, now I was under the impression, that the Embrace does bestow certain improvements and healing on the body, else that people that are riddled with war wounds and pre death injuries could impact the kindred 's life. For most Kindred the brace removed infirmities and healed old nagging wounds, infact missing limbs would regrow. Else some one undergoing emergency transformation could be stuck as a pile of hamburger or just riddled with the tumors that stricken them.<br /> <br /> My goto evidence is good old AL Capote, who was rendered a syphlitic idiot during his stay in prison because he refused to get a shot. But by the time we meet him, his mental faculties are back to full, restored by the vitae <br /> <br /> How do you guys run it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T22:18:54-08:00","id":1471178,"title":"","content":"I run it as whatever is most dramatically appropriate for the story. Even in prior editions it was never consistent. Sometimes it healed injuries and conditions, sometimes it didn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T23:50:53-08:00","id":1471180,"title":"","content":"My take has always been that the beast wants its shell to be as powerful as possible. So it repairs its shell and improves it slightly, at least by a predator's definition of &quot;improve&quot;. Fangs grow, appearance gets sexier, minor defects get fixed, that sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-23T23:56:02-08:00","id":1471181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1471176-effects-of-the-embrace-and-regeneration?p=1471178#post1471178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I run it as whatever is most dramatically appropriate for the story. Even in prior editions it was never consistent. Sometimes it healed injuries and conditions, sometimes it didn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>This effectively.<br /> <br /> All we know is the embrace takes time, a few weeks, to fully solidify. During the first few hours the new Cainite experiences a burning sensation as all the none blood liquids are purged. The next few days are when a major changes occur if at all. Most of the time, the blood effectively locks people in place after the embrace. However, thinner blood seems to be much more pronounced when it comes to random mutations during the finalization stage.<br /> <br /> Side note, most weaknesses develop in the coming weeks, particularly subjective ones like the Ventrue and Nosferatu curse. Some occur almost instantly like the Malkavian and Brujah curses.<br /> <br /> The information is purposely inconsistent and incomplete so STs can change it up as they see fit. The general rule is the embrace often keeps you in the same state as when you died. The few exceptions tend to be seemingly random, as if the blood worked in the sense of mutations and evolution. Theoretically in a mass embrace situation, these would be a lot more common mutations and caitiff variations. Saving that idea for later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}